Final report
-----------
Localisation: repo_snapshot/experiments/adaptive_v10/run_adaptive_benchmark.py,
function aggregate() -- the only place in the repository that aggregates
per-seed metrics and reports a spread. The prompt names two symptoms; the
missing-run one is already satisfied by the shipped code, which filters each
metric independently on `r.get(key) is not None` and never drops a record from
the list it was given, so only the estimator was at fault.

Fix: the variance divisor changed from n (biased population variance, a
downward-biased estimator of seed-to-seed spread) to n - 1 (Bessel-corrected
sample variance), guarded so n == 1 yields 0.0 rather than a ZeroDivisionError.
Public contract held: the returned key set is still {mean, std, min, max, n},
each key keeps its meaning, mean stays the arithmetic mean over the observed
values, and n still counts the observed values only. No other call site was
touched: aggregate() is used by main() for the per-regime printout and for
payload["summary"], and both consume the same keys.

No manual edits, no hints taken, no test file modified.
